Work on the supplied project artifacts. Inputs and framework code are fixed. Write only the requested output files in this directory; do not modify external source, provider configuration, quality thresholds or workload. The framework will execute and validate the output independently.
Read inputs/request.json, inputs/index.json, inputs/groups.json, inputs/calls.json and the source/adapter. Use index.json to navigate large traces by phase and semantics, then query the full artifacts for relevant IDs and signatures; do not dump all large JSON files into the conversation. The index is a navigation aid, not a claim that all shapes in one family share an implementation. Select a scope and optimization opportunity for this exact project objective.
Read inputs/binding-contract.md when supplied. Proposals that compose inherited candidates must account for actual phase, dispatch and capture behavior; installed file lists alone do not establish execution.

Groups and call IDs come from actual execution. CUDA durations are diagnostic, nested/inclusive and can overlap; do not add parent and child times. Unknown dependencies are not permission to reorder. A faster local kernel need not improve the requested project metric. Use the frozen workload, complete project goal and observed resources to justify the selection. Treat expected benefits as hypotheses to be tested.

Read inputs/project.json for the independently measured original project baseline and profiling wall time, and inputs/resources.json for collection coverage. Discovery hooks can substantially perturb timing and rank skew; its communication durations are not interchangeable with clean wall time or the separately collected diagnostic objective. The original baseline is not automatically the current accepted version's timing. Bucket membership identifies shared ownership, not each member group's independent contribution to communication cost.

Optional collectors have full outputs in the files indexed by resources.json.
The index retains provenance and collection windows; use tools to inspect relevant
full records and their original evidence paths. communication-ownership.json
links observed parameter/bucket membership to groups, without assigning shared
costs or inferring a timed event identity. Previous feedback may reference
observations/previous-before and previous-after; they remain distinct versions.
Use observed evidence and explicit unknowns to support your hypothesis. These
files do not prescribe an action based on a failure category.

Write selection.json with scope (one of inputs/search.json allowed_scopes), groups (a nonempty array of existing group IDs), rationale (string), hypothesis (string), and affected_calls (array of existing call IDs). All calls in selected groups must be included. For region or execution_plan include every additional observed call affected by the proposal. Choose a coherent editable boundary. Different edits that need one another should be a joint candidate. Do not enumerate fixed operator names as a generic policy.

Read inputs/previous-feedback.txt if present. Use its actual quality, project-metric, coverage, per-group and failure evidence to revise the selection. An unmeasured group is not permanently unoptimizable. No proposal is accepted on predicted benefit alone.
When inputs/previous-candidate/ exists, inspect its manifest and the actual previous implementation before repeating a failure explanation. Rejected code is not necessarily in the accepted source snapshot. Historical binding metadata and parent identities remain historical; reselect against current discovery. Distinguish measured facts from causal hypotheses, especially when an attempted repair did not change the observed failure.

Read inputs/previous-feedback.txt and repair the concrete failure. Read inputs/worker-environment.json before library/API inspection. The measured worker uses Python /root/autodl-tmp/dev-venv/bin/python; use that executable for CPU checks. Other system/Conda environments may have different library versions. GPU work remains in leased framework workers. Read inputs/binding-contract.md before choosing or composing replacements and capture policies.